MEDICAL DATA ANALYSIS WITH PYTHON


This project focuses on processing, cleaning, analyzing, and visualizing medical data using Python. The goal is to extract meaningful insights from patient records and support data-driven understanding of health conditions such as diabetes, blood metrics, and therapy effectiveness.

The project demonstrates a full data pipeline:

Data insertion & loading

Data cleaning & preprocessing

Exploratory data analysis (EDA)

Statistical insights

Data visualization


FEATURES

Import and manage patient datasets

Clean missing, inconsistent, or noisy data

Analyze medical indicators (glucose, hemoglobin, etc.)

Visualize trends and comparisons

Extract insights based on disease duration, condition, and therapy type


TECHNOLOGIES USED

-Python 3.x

-pandas

-numpy

-matplotlib / seaborn

-Jupyter Notebook


EXAMPLE ANALYSIS 

Diabetes & Glucose Levels

- Analyze average glucose levels in patients diagnosed with diabetes

- Filter by duration of the disease, type of therapy, glucose or hemoglobin A1C

- Identify trends and potential risk patterns

- Compare diabetic retinopathy in patients with different kind of therapy

